  "notes": "SNB quarterly Financial Data Supplement (.xlsx, SAR mn). Raw reported lines only; the supplement's own ratios (NPL, coverage, CASA, Tier 1, CAR, LCR, NSFR, LDR, RoTE, NIM, cost-to-income, cost of risk) are not mapped - regulatory capital comes from the Pillar 3 KM1 reader and every other ratio is recomputed by the engine. Values are rounded to the issuer's reported precision (thousands of SAR = 3 decimals in SAR mn; EPS to 2 decimals) because formula cells carry binary float noise. 'Depreciation and amortization' is deliberately not mapped: the supplement line includes amortisation of intangible assets (FY2024 SAR 2,608.054 mn) while the audited statement's depreciation_amortization excludes it (FY2024 SAR 1,787,774 thousand), so it is a different definition, not a restatement. 'Earnings per share' maps to eps_diluted because SNB's reviewed statements print identical basic and diluted EPS. The non-controlling-interest income row is printed as a deduction (sign inverted relative to the statements) and is negated.",
